  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Show that $\\dfrac54<2^{1/3}<\\dfrac43$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac54\\right)^3=\\dfrac{125}{64}<2<\\dfrac{64}{27}=\\left(\\dfrac43\\right)^3$.\n\nTaking cube roots gives $\\dfrac54<2^{1/3}<\\dfrac43$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac54\\right)^3&=\\frac{125}{64}<\\frac{128}{64}=2\\\\\\left(\\frac43\\right)^3&=\\frac{64}{27}>\\frac{54}{27}=2\\end{align*}$$\nThe cube function is increasing, so taking cube roots preserves these inequalities. Therefore $\\dfrac54<2^{1/3}<\\dfrac43$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
